# Reference examples for resource conventions and authorization. Run the app with the Development profile.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:5001

# Paste an access token from Keycloak (e.g. Scalar's OAuth2 flow, or a client-credentials request).
@token = paste-a-token-here

### Layering: check X-Level-App/Group/Endpoint (all "true") and X-Configured-By ("endpoint")
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/layers/headers

### Versioning: same route, version 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/v2/demo/layers/headers

### Authenticated: 401 without a token
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/authenticated

### Authenticated: with a token, lists your claims (handy to see how Keycloak sends roles and scopes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/authenticated
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Scope "api.read": 403 if the token lacks it
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/scope
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Role "admin" (Keycloak realm or client role, or a plain role claim, depending on IdentityProvider:Provider): 403 without it
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Combined: needs scope "api.write" AND role "admin"
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/combined
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### API key: local key from appsettings.json works on "either" (scope api.read comes from the key's settings)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/either
X-Api-Key: local-dev-api-key

### Bearer token works on "either" too (needs scope api.read)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/either
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Wrong API key -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/either
X-Api-Key: wrong-key

### API key only: API key with role "reader" -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/api-key-only
X-Api-Key: local-dev-api-key

### API key only: a bearer token alone -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/api-key-only
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Bearer only: an API key alone -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/auth/bearer-only
X-Api-Key: local-dev-api-key

### ---- Diagnostics, dependencies and policies ----

### Health: live -> 200 with name and version
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Health: ready -> 200, status only (no dependency names)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

### Health: status without a token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/status

### Correlation: the response echoes this id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/diagnostics/correlation
Correlation-Id: my-test-correlation-id

### Correlation: invalid id (space and "!") -> a new one is generated
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/diagnostics/correlation
Correlation-Id: not valid!

### Typed client (IGitHubClient on the GitHub dependency): 200 with the user, 404 for an unknown one
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/dependencies/github/octocat

### Named client from IHttpClientFactory (RandomUser): forwards Correlation-Id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/dependencies/random-user
Correlation-Id: forwarded-to-random-user

### Rate limiting: send 4 times within 10 seconds; the 4th returns 429 with Retry-After
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/rate-limiting/limited

### Timeout: 1 second -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/timeouts/1

### Timeout: 5 seconds -> 504 after ~2 seconds (not enforced while debugging)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/timeouts/5

### Idempotency: send twice -> same id both times
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/idempotency/orders
Idempotency-Key: test-key-0001

### Idempotency: different key -> different id
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/idempotency/orders
Idempotency-Key: test-key-0002

### Errors: 500 ProblemDetails, no stack trace in the body
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/diagnostics/error

### Authorization: 401 without a token
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/diagnostics/authorized

### Security headers: check X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options and Referrer-Policy on the response
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Output cache (policy "short", 10 seconds): the timestamp stays the same for 10 seconds
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/caching/timestamp

### Unknown route -> 404 with a problem body
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nothing-here

### Pagination: second page of 5, ordered by name descending then id
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/pagination/people?page=2&pageSize=5&orderBy=name:desc&orderBy=id

### Pagination: created range (from inclusive, to exclusive) and a name filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/pagination/people?createdFrom=2026-02-10T00:00:00Z&createdTo=2026-02-13T00:00:00Z&name=person

### Pagination: 400 for a page size over the maximum, an unknown order field, and a backwards range (all reported together)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/pagination/people?pageSize=1000&orderBy=secret&createdFrom=2026-02-01T00:00:00Z&createdTo=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z

### Cursor pagination: first page; copy nextCursor from the response into the next call (same filters and ordering)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/pagination/people/stream?pageSize=10&orderBy=name:desc

### Cursor pagination: next page (paste the cursor); a cursor with other filters returns 400 pagination.cursor_mismatch
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/demo/pagination/people/stream?pageSize=10&orderBy=name:desc&cursor=PASTE_NEXT_CURSOR_HERE
